# tools/ales_stereo_gate_env_hold_witness.rish — stereo_gate_env_hold: the attack/hold/release noise gate carried into stereo, the linked held envelope driving one linked gate over time (ALES167).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES167.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-072727_fill-ales167-lotus-stereo-gate-env-hold.md
# Stands on: lotus/stereo_hold_env.rye (ALES165 — the linked held follower, its stereo_env_step_hold reused whole), lotus/stereo_gate_env.rye (ALES162 — the un-held linked gate this reduces to at a hold of zero),
# lotus/gate_env_hold.rye (ALES57 — the mono attack/hold/release gate, its GateEnvHoldError reused whole and its output the left-always-peak comparison), lotus/gate.rye (ALES51 — the silenced floor), lotus/pan.rye
# (ALES10 — the StereoClip), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, sample_max, max_clip).
#
# lotus/stereo_gate_env_hold.rye gates a span of sample-PAIRS in a master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward push following the shared LINKED HELD envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared
# envelope with one shared hold countdown toward the linked peak max(|left|, |right|) by ALES165's step (attack while rising and rearming the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, release once it expires):
# at or above the threshold both pass byte for byte, below it the silenced floor gat = e·den/num (ALES51's floor on the linked held envelope) yields one gain gat/e applied to both raw samples — one detector, one hold, one
# gate, the image held. GateEnvHoldError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole; the fusion adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the zero-hold law (a hold of zero reducing it to
# ALES162's stereo_gate_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held one already proven), the linked-gate-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with left' equal to ALES57's mono
# gate_env_hold(left), the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel gate_env_hold differing), the image law (the shared gain preserving the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase),
# the knob / no-chatter laws (unit ratio the identity, a nonzero hold keeping the gate open across a dip rather than chattering), the carry law (a span in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to the whole once on both, env
# and hold_left carrying), and the above-threshold/silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_gate_env_hold_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: Language EN — stereo_gate_env_hold gates a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, the one downward push following the shared linked held envelope over time. Each pair advances one shared envelope with one shared hold countdown toward the linked peak (the max of the two channels' magnitudes, clamped to the rail): the attack fraction while it rises and rearms the shared hold, the peak pinned while the countdown lasts, the release only once it expires; where the held envelope sits at or above the threshold the gate is open and both channels pass byte for byte, and where it falls below, the envelope's whole magnitude is divided by the ratio and the single gain (the silenced floor over the envelope) is applied to both raw samples. It validates the threshold, ratio, attack, release, hold, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never gates one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; the caller owns the envelope and the countdown across calls, so a span gated in two pieces equals the whole once even when the split falls mid-hold."
say "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: Style Radiant — ALES162 carried the breathing gate into stereo: one shared envelope opening as a sound arrives and closing gently as it falls away, one silenced gain applied to both channels so the image never lurches. Yet an un-held gate still slams shut and re-opens on a brief dip between two loud samples — it chatters, and the ear hears the door swing on the whole field at once. A real gate carries a hold knob for exactly this: on a fall away from a peak, it pins the peak for a little while before the release begins, so the gate stays open through the dip and the passage stays whole. ALES165 built that hold stage inside the linked follower and proved it once. This rung spends that proof: it drives ALES51's silenced floor from the linked held envelope rather than the plain linked one — the same stereo gate, now with the patience that keeps it from chattering the image. It is the stereo mirror of ALES57's held mono gate. Two proofs fused: the detector is the linked held follower (one shared envelope, one shared hold countdown pinning the linked peak across a fall so the two channels never re-open on different samples), and the gate is linked (one silenced gain from the linked held envelope applied to both). The crux is six laws: the zero-hold law (a hold of zero making the linked held follower the plain linked follower, so this equals ALES162's stereo_gate_env byte for byte on both — the held rung's no-hold limit exactly the un-held rung already proven); the linked-gate-over-time law (a left-always-peak master with the left equal to ALES57's mono gate_env_hold of it byte for byte, the right scaled by the same fraction, the independent per-channel gate_env_hold genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserving the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the knob and no-chatter laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, and a nonzero hold keeping the gate open across a brief dip — the held magnitude no smaller than the un-held one and strictly louder at the dip, the chatter avoided); the carry law (a span gated in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to gating the whole once, byte for byte on both); and the above-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a master whose linked held envelope never falls below the threshold passing byte for byte, silence staying silence, the lengths held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) carrying one shared i64 envelope and one shared u32 hold countdown, one linked-peak comparison and at most one multiply-then-divide for the held envelope step (ALES165's proven stereo_env_step_hold) plus one per channel for the gain, all in i64 (the product of a magnitude and the silenced floor at most 32768 times 32767 never overflowing), the gain gat over e in the closed interval zero to one so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's and fits i16; the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (a gate writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit, each written sign asserted held); the threshold, ratio, both coefficients, the hold, and the span are validated once before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never gates one channel and leaves the other torn; a zero held envelope is asserted to arise only when both channels are silent this pair, so there is no divide by zero, and the silenced floor is asserted within zero to the envelope so the single gain is a genuine reduction; StereoGateEnvHoldError is ALES57's GateEnvHoldError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadCoeff, BadHold, BadRange) reused whole, the fusion adding no fault. The zero-hold law is proven by running both stereo_gate_env_hold under a hold of zero and ALES162's un-held stereo_gate_env on the same master and demanding byte-for-byte equality on both channels; the linked-gate-over-time law against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to ALES57's mono gate_env_hold of it byte for byte while the right is scaled by the same fraction, the independent mono gate_env_hold of the right alone shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase pair returns still exactly out of phase; the knob and no-chatter laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere and a nonzero hold keeping the gate open across a dip where an un-held gate chatters; the carry law proves a span gated in two pieces, the split mid-hold, equal to the whole once on both channels; and the above-threshold, silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an always-loud master passing byte for byte, an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the five refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units, the ratio a plain fraction, the attack, release, and hold per sample index, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_gate_env_hold"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_gate_env_hold.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_gate_env_hold.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-gate-env-hold' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-gate-env-hold: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-gate-env-hold line"
